diagnosis_text:
I cannot reproduce the outage. The inter-domain routing between the “two sides” (OSPF on the pc0 side and EIGRP on the pc12 side) is operating correctly, and end-to-end connectivity is healthy now.

Evidence:
- From pc0 to pc12: 5/5 ICMP replies, 0% loss, ~0.96 ms RTT, TTL 61, confirming a 3-hop path.
- From pc12 to pc0: 2/2 ICMP replies, 0% loss, ~1.28 ms RTT.
- r1’s routing table resolves 120.0.0.0/8 via r11 over OSPF (show ip route 120.1.1.10 → via 111.1.1.2 on eth1), confirming successful OSPF import of the EIGRP-learned network.
- r11 is configured to run both EIGRP (AS 100) and OSPF, redistributing EIGRP into OSPF as the handoff between domains.
- r12 runs EIGRP for 120.0.0.0/8 and has a default route to r11 (K>* 0.0.0.0/0 via 112.1.1.1), so return traffic is correctly steered.

Localization and mechanism: Traffic flows pc0 → r1 (E) → r11 (B) → r12 (EE) → pc12 (GG), with EIGRP↔OSPF redistribution on r11. Route availability and ICMP success show the transport and control planes are normal.

Root cause: No current fault found; the issue is not reproducible. It may have been transient or application/host-level rather than network.

Corrective fix: No changes required. Please retest your specific application/port; if it still times out, provide the protocol/port so we can test beyond ICMP and trace any host/service firewall issues. We can also enable temporary route/adjacency monitoring if intermittent symptoms recur.
